4. Ears. — Pain behind r. ear. — Tearing from r. cheek-bone to ears and around ears extending to upper part of occiput along lamboidal suture. —Sensation in both ears as if wind were rushing out. — Loss of hearing during cough. — Roaring as of a distant wind-storm.

5. Nose. — Tip swollen and red. — Dry coryza with (one-sided) stoppage. —Fluent CGryza. — Discharge of black blood with mucus on waking in morning.—Obstrnction with liver complaints. — Hallucinations of smell (on stooping).

6. Face. — Red without heat. — Remarkably yellow, esp. forehead, nose, and cheeks. — The usual red has a mixture of dark yellow. — Tension and drawing in (1.) malar bone. — Sensation of swelling in r. cheek-bones. — Burrowing-tearing in antrum. — Itching in face and on forehead. — Herpes on face, esp. chin. — Lips swollen; dry, cracked, crusty, feeling.

