15. Male Sexual Organs. — Penis painful, with redness of the glans, and lancinations in the urethra. — Pullings in the 1. spermatic cord, hindering walking.— L. testicle retracted, the r. pendant, and flaccid.-— Tetter-like eruption on the scrotum. — Erections.

16. Female Sexual Organs. — Catamenia too scanty, or altogether suppressed, with dyspnoea and palpitation of the heart, e^p. on going to bed. — Pain and stitches through the breasts into the chest, and extending to the back, as soon as the child begins to nurse.

