ord lay under the skin. Prostration is present as with the other Euphorbias; but Euphorbium has, in addition, periodic cramp, writer's cramp, and convulsions with loss of consciousness. Most symptoms are < at night and in the morning. Rest <, motion >. Pau^ytic weakness in joints < on beginning to move. Painfulness of coccyx, < on rising from sitting. Heat <; cool applications >. Touch <.

