, and itches very much, esp. when walking in the open air. — Abundant desquamation of the scalp. — Falling off of the hair, even on the sides of the head and the whiskers. — Rheumatic pains in the scalp, principally in the sides, extending to the teeth and cervical glands; < when walking and becoming cold in open air, > from warmth and while getting warm when walking. — Perspiration smelling acid or very offensive, colouring the linen yellow; on the head (as on the whole body) at night and during the day, from the least exercise; < even while talking, > when walking in the open air. — The hair turns grey.

