» 6. Face.— Heat in face, sometimes after a meal, and with thirst. — Dryness and constriction of skin of face and eyelids as though covered with a thin layer of albumen; cheeks look glazed and contracted. — Pale, yellowish complexion. — Facial paralysis (from inflammatory products in Fallopian canal). — Eruption of pimples on face, — Scurfs around mouth. — Scabby pimples, with shooting pain on lips, and commissures. — Furuncles on lower lip. — Swelling of 'Sub-maxillary glands. — Easy dislocation jf maxillary joint in bed in morning with sharp pains.

