umatism. These pains were icy cold, as if produced by an extremely fine ice-cold needle. As Sac. 1. has fine cold pains ” and pains passing in all directions, Sac. /. im was gtven, and relieved all the pains within an hour. {Sac. 0^. has cold expectoration.”) The symptoms are < before a storm; in damp room or basement; morning and evening; by blue and yellow colours; exertion; mental excitement. > By warmth of fire; by red colour; after 4 p.m.

